Z||000003||Mattsfiero||04-18-2001||09:35 PM||||The back up light switch is located on the top of the Transmission block. I had mine go bad and had to replace the switch already. That might be the problem. Get back to me and let me know how it turns out. No pun intended. I will double check the wires and let you know what colors you are looking for when I have light here tommorow.<P>------------------<BR>Matt<BR>85 custom coupe<BR>Mattsfiero@aol.com<BR>www.anglefire.com/ma3/mattsfiero||||reg||1
Z||000004||sqoach||04-19-2001||02:59 PM||||So, I should go to the parts store and ask for a back-up light switch?||||reg||1
Z||000005||286SE'S||04-19-2001||03:08 PM||||you can pull the connector to the switch and put a wire jumper across two connectors on the cable end. Turn the ignition on and the lights should come on. That proves it is the switch. You need a special open sided socket to get it out as the cable runs into the switch. It is in an awful place to get to.<BR>I think the socket is called an oxygen sensor type.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Tigger||04-19-2001||03:26 PM||||Try this sqoach,<P><A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/008751.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/008751.html</A><P>Could be the switch in the center console needs to be adjusted.<p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 04-19-2001).]||||reg||1
